	<main class="page-width page-main"><div class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">HELP & FAQ</p><h1>Good to know</h1><p>Quick answers about submitting a concern and following what happens next.</p></div>
		<section class="form-panel" style="max-width:800px">
			<article class="faq-item"><h2>What can I report?</h2><p>Everyday community concerns such as roads and walkways, waste, street lighting, public spaces, drainage, or safety. For immediate danger or emergencies, contact local emergency services.</p></article>
			<article class="faq-item"><h2>How do I track a report?</h2><p>After submission, save the reference code shown on screen. Enter it in the tracker on the <a class="text-link" href="reports.php">community reports page</a> to find its latest status and leader update.</p></article>
			<article class="faq-item"><h2>Are my name and phone number public?</h2><p>No. Your account name is shared privately with community leaders so they can follow up, and your phone number is optional. Neither is displayed in the public report list. The report title, description, category, and location are public, so avoid including sensitive personal details in those fields.</p></article>
			<article class="faq-item"><h2>What do the report statuses mean?</h2><p>“Reported” means it has been submitted. “In review” means a leader is assessing it. “In progress” means follow-up work is underway. “Resolved” means the leader has marked the issue complete.</p></article>
			<article class="faq-item"><h2>Can I edit a report after submitting it?</h2><p>Reports cannot currently be edited by residents. If important details change, submit a new report and mention the earlier reference code in the description.</p></article>
			<article class="faq-item"><h2>How do community leaders access reports?</h2><p>Leaders sign in to their protected dashboard, where they can review submissions, change a status, and share a public progress update.</p></article>
